--------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project contains no third-party source code or assets.

That is a deliberate state rather than a lucky one, and it is worth recording
what was removed to reach it:

facesjs — https://github.com/zengm-games/facesjs
    REMOVED. faceSvgs.js bundled a curated subset of the facesjs SVG feature
    artwork (161 path elements, ~136KB) together with a renderer ported from
    their approach. None of it was reachable: player likenesses are drawn by
    ui/pixelSprites.js, and the only values any caller ever read off a face
    descriptor were a skin colour and a hair colour. The artwork, the
    renderer, the generator script (scripts/build-face-svgs.js) and the
    retained licence file have all been deleted. faces.js now does nothing but
    pick those two colours.

ZenGM (basketball-gm) — https://github.com/zengm-games/zengm
    Never included. No ZenGM source code has been copied into this repository.
    It is cited in comments in compositeRatings.js and draftLotteryFormats.js
    as the source of an APPROACH, and in calibration comments as the source of
    the real-NBA statistics some constants were fitted against. Attribution of
    an idea and of public data, not of code.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A NOTE ON TEAMS, LOGOS AND ROSTER DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

TEAMS ARE FICTIONAL. The thirty clubs in teams.js are invented. Each keeps a
real city, because market size and prestige are modelled against real market
realities and would be arbitrary numbers attached to invented places — but no
club name, nickname or mark belongs to any real team.

NO LOGOS ARE DISTRIBUTED. assets/logos/ ships empty by design. The UI renders
a colored badge built from each team's own palette, and will use a logo file
only if someone adds one themselves. See assets/logos/README.md.

ROSTER DATA IS REAL. players-2026.js contains real player names together with
attribute ratings. Those names belong to the players themselves; the ratings
are this project's own assessments, not any league's or publisher's. They are
used descriptively, no ownership of any person's name or likeness is claimed,
and no endorsement or affiliation with any player, club or league is implied
or should be inferred.

Anyone redistributing this, or building anything commercial on it, should
satisfy themselves about that last paragraph independently. A licence covers
copyright in the code; it does not grant rights in anybody's name.
